# trusted-owner-ids — owner-mode allowlist for the merge path (PHNX-3950).
#
# One numeric GitHub USER id per line ('#' starts a comment). An agent whose
# authenticated `gh api user` id is listed here gets "owner-mode": its own
# code-reviewer APPROVE clears pr-verdict.py even though the whole fleet shares
# one GitHub login (see hooks/lib/owner-mode.sh and pr-verdict.py). Every other
# gate — real-word APPROVE, no carried-from laundering, no negated/quoted
# approvals, CI-green (enforced by GitHub) — still applies, and --admin stays
# blocked; owner-mode only stops the guard/auto-merger from false-blocking the
# ONE identity the repo ruleset already exempts server-side.
#
# THIS FILE SHIPS EMPTY. The upstream mirror grants no fleet by default. Opt
# YOUR fleet in WITHOUT editing this shared file (the system layer is a pull-only
# mirror — local edits here are overwritten on the next `agents repo pull
# system`). Instead use either:
#   * ${HOME}/.agents/trusted-owner-ids  (user layer; survives mirror pulls), or
#   * export AGENTS_MERGE_TRUSTED_OWNER_IDS="<id> <id>"  in the fleet env.
# Find your id with:  gh api user --jq .id
